  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would, by virtue of the cumulative impact of its internal layout deficiencies result in substandard accommodation overall. These combined shortcomings would fail to provide a satisfactory quality of living environment and would be incapable of meeting the reasonable day-to-day needs of future occupiers in terms of functionality contrary to the requirement to secure high-quality residential environments and  Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies, D3, D4, D5 and D6 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD6, DMD8, DMD9 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) and the London Housing Supplementary Planning Guidance (2016).",
    "The proposed cycle storage, by virtue of its means of access, location and layout would fail to provide a secure, convenient and high quality facility for all types of bicycles and would fail to promote or prioritise  the use of sustainable modes of transport, contrary to Section 9 of the National Planning Policy  Framework (2021), Policies T2, T3, T4, T6, and T6.1 of the London Plan (2021), CP25 of  the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD45, DMD47 and DMD48 of the Enfield Development  Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed change of use to a House in Multiple Occupation (HMO), by virtue of the prominence of waste storage and required cycle storage on the site frontage would result in an over-intensive form of development that would erode the established residential character and appearance of the area. The proposal is therefore contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies DMD5 and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), and Core Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010).",
    "The proposed development would by virtue of the requirement to accommodate cycle and refuse storage on the site frontage results in the loss of a parking space.  In this low PTAL (1B) location with a lack of off street parking, the Local Planning Authority is not satisfied that the surrounding highway network has the capacity to accommodate the resultant demand to the detriment of highway conditions and the character of the area, contrary to section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (2021), and Policies DMD5 (d), DMD45 and DMD47 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
